freebsd-timeline manages ZFS snapshots, boot environments and backups.

A small root daemon takes snapshots on a schedule and prunes them with
hourly, daily, weekly and monthly retention. A CLI and a GTK4/libadwaita
desktop app show every snapshot on a timeline and can browse, diff and roll
back to any of them, manage bectl boot environments, report pool health,
lock encrypted datasets, and send raw incremental backups over SSH to a
machine you own.

freebsd-timeline has no accounts, no telemetry and opens no network ports.
